&lt;i&gt;Big boobs, small boobs,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny boobs and middle-size boobs&lt;/i&gt;

9
00:00:35,106 --> 00:00:37,900
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!&lt;/i&gt;

10
00:00:38,109 --> 00:00:40,903
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:00:41,112 --> 00:00:43,906
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:00:44,115 --> 00:00:46,742
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

13
00:00:46,951 --> 00:00:49,412
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;it's here already!&lt;/i&gt;

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:52,623
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

15
00:00:52,832 --> 00:00:55,460
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

16
00:00:55,668 --> 00:00:58,463
&lt;i&gt;Big butts, small butts,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny butts and middle-size butts&lt;/i&gt;

17
00:00:58,671 --> 00:01:02,967
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Bounce, bounce, bounce!&lt;/i&gt;

18
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:14,896
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,486
&lt;i&gt;Bouncing at the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggling at the beach&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:01:23,321 --> 00:01:24,322
&lt;i&gt;Want you!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:01:28,159 --> 00:01:34,040
FOOD CART BUSINESS FLYING HIGH!

22
00:01:40,588 --> 00:01:42,507
What the heck is this?

23
00:01:42,715 --> 00:01:44,675
"Leaving application"?

24
00:01:44,926 --> 00:01:45,718
Huh?

25
00:01:45,927 --> 00:01:48,513
Leaving? You're leaving us?

26
00:01:48,721 --> 00:01:49,555
What?

27
00:01:50,264 --> 00:01:52,391
Quit joking, Chief!

28
00:01:52,642 --> 00:01:56,187
It's meant to say "Leave Application."

29
00:01:56,395 --> 00:01:57,688
You idiot!!

30
00:01:58,773 --> 00:02:01,692
You're an adult and you can't even write kanji properly!

31
00:02:01,901 --> 00:02:04,904
Are you taking a day off to go on a date?

32
00:02:05,112 --> 00:02:06,072
I doubt it.

33
00:02:06,614 --> 00:02:09,826
The reason is written inside, sir.

34
00:02:10,201 --> 00:02:11,118
Huh?

35
00:02:13,746 --> 00:02:14,580
"Reason."

36
00:02:14,789 --> 00:02:15,581
Hmm?

37
00:02:16,207 --> 00:02:20,127
"To enjoy Kameari Firework Festival. Signed: Kankichi Ryotsu"

38
00:02:21,546 --> 00:02:25,091
I've been a firework freak since I was a kid, Chief.

39
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,051
You idiot!!

40
00:02:28,052 --> 00:02:31,681
Don't you know what your job is?

41
00:02:32,181 --> 00:02:34,433
Of course I know. I'm a police officer!

42
00:02:34,642 --> 00:02:39,564
And you think a police officer can take a day off for a firework festival?

43
00:02:39,772 --> 00:02:43,317
There's a huge crowd every year.

44
00:02:43,526 --> 00:02:45,945
We'll be so busy policing.

45
00:02:46,195 --> 00:02:47,572
Correct.

46
00:02:48,114 --> 00:02:51,325
Huh, all right. I'll just skip work instead...

47
00:02:51,534 --> 00:02:54,245
Then I will fire your ass!

48
00:02:54,453 --> 00:02:56,455
I was just joking!

49
00:03:02,587 --> 00:03:07,008
The chief is so bullheaded, always working us to the bone.

50
00:03:09,176 --> 00:03:13,014
I wish I could watch the fireworks from up there.

51
00:03:13,723 --> 00:03:18,102
Damn it! There must be some way I can get the day off!

52
00:03:18,311 --> 00:03:19,979
Hey, Ryo-san!

53
00:03:20,187 --> 00:03:20,980
Huh?

54
00:03:21,397 --> 00:03:22,189
Hi there.

55
00:03:22,398 --> 00:03:23,190
Oh!

56
00:03:23,399 --> 00:03:28,571
I'd was just on my way to pay my tab. I swear!

57
00:03:33,451 --> 00:03:35,411
Can't give him money I don't have.

58
00:03:35,953 --> 00:03:36,746
Huh?

59
00:03:44,629 --> 00:03:46,297
Are times really that hard?

60
00:03:46,547 --> 00:03:51,636
Yeah. Even what you just paid me won't make any difference.

61
00:03:52,303 --> 00:03:53,638
I'm one step from this.

62
00:03:54,263 --> 00:03:56,432
But with so many new apartment buildings,

63
00:03:56,641 --> 00:03:59,226
you should be getting lots of new customers.

64
00:03:59,685 --> 00:04:03,356
They can't even hear my jingle from all the way up there.

65
00:04:04,023 --> 00:04:07,735
Why not take orders over the phone and deliver?

66
00:04:08,152 --> 00:04:11,072
I'm on my own, so I can't leave my cart.

67
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:14,367
And it's not as if I can drag it into an elevator.

68
00:04:14,742 --> 00:04:17,995
And helicopter deliveries would cost too much,

69
00:04:18,204 --> 00:04:20,498
not to mention the engine noise.

70
00:04:20,706 --> 00:04:22,249
There must be a way...

71
00:04:30,466 --> 00:04:31,384
Aha!

72
00:04:41,602 --> 00:04:43,396
Ooh yeah!

73
00:04:44,230 --> 00:04:45,439
Easy does it.

74
00:04:47,858 --> 00:04:50,903
What's up, Katsushika Balloon Club?

75
00:04:51,487 --> 00:04:53,197
Hi, Ryo-san.

76
00:04:53,406 --> 00:04:55,825
This is a new balloon, isn't it?

77
00:04:56,033 --> 00:04:57,743
Yeah, went into debt to get it.

78
00:04:57,952 --> 00:04:58,953
Where's the old one?

79
00:04:59,161 --> 00:05:00,913
We shoved it in storage.

80
00:05:01,706 --> 00:05:03,708
Would you mind lending it to me?

81
00:05:03,916 --> 00:05:06,419
My friend wants to see it.

82
00:05:06,877 --> 00:05:10,339
Sure, we're always glad to have some new balloon buddies.

83
00:05:10,548 --> 00:05:11,424
Go ahead.

84
00:05:11,632 --> 00:05:14,385
&lt;i&gt;KATSUSHIKA BALLOON CLUB&lt;/i&gt;

85
00:05:19,974 --> 00:05:22,768
You want me to deliver ramen in this?

86
00:05:22,977 --> 00:05:26,105
You can use propane gas to cook and fly at the same time.

87
00:05:26,313 --> 00:05:29,400
Oh, you're suggesting I cook in here too...

88
00:05:29,608 --> 00:05:30,526
How's it look?

89
00:05:30,735 --> 00:05:34,697
Huh? Oh, right. My buddy here is very impressed.

90
00:05:34,905 --> 00:05:37,783
In fact, he was just saying he'd love to go for a ride.

91
00:05:38,492 --> 00:05:39,910
Yes, please.

92
00:05:40,286 --> 00:05:43,164
Well then, how about right now?

93
00:05:48,586 --> 00:05:50,171
It's taking shape!

94
00:05:50,379 --> 00:05:52,423
Get all the steps in your head.

95
00:05:52,631 --> 00:05:54,175
What? Why?

96
00:05:54,383 --> 00:05:58,095
Because when the time comes, we're gonna be doing this on our own.

97
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,974
Won't the bearded guy be with us?

98
00:06:02,475 --> 00:06:07,188
Do you really think he'd help us turn his balloon into a food cart?

99
00:06:08,481 --> 00:06:12,777
Plus, flying hot air balloons at night isn't allowed in Japan.

100
00:06:12,985 --> 00:06:16,781
What if he finds out our plan?

101
00:06:17,782 --> 00:06:22,328
He's as wild as his beard. He might bite us to death.

102
00:06:22,536 --> 00:06:23,704
What?!

103
00:06:26,499 --> 00:06:28,667
Guys, get on! Quick!

104
00:06:29,085 --> 00:06:30,586
Okay... Oops!

105
00:06:31,378 --> 00:06:33,047
Take it easy now.

106
00:06:35,341 --> 00:06:36,675
We're flying!

107
00:06:37,051 --> 00:06:39,637
That's professional, bravo!

108
00:06:40,304 --> 00:06:44,517
The balloon is controlled by adjusting these burners.

109
00:06:44,725 --> 00:06:47,144
It can go way up high...

110
00:06:47,394 --> 00:06:51,148
No need for that. The height of an apartment block will do.

111
00:06:51,357 --> 00:06:52,149
What?

112
00:06:52,358 --> 00:06:53,984
Oh, nothing!

113
00:06:55,694 --> 00:06:58,906
To descend rapidly, release some hot air.

114
00:06:59,114 --> 00:07:00,991
Release hot air...

115
00:07:01,367 --> 00:07:03,202
Wow, you're very keen.

116
00:07:03,410 --> 00:07:05,913
His livelihood depends on this after all.

117
00:07:06,121 --> 00:07:06,914
Livelihood?

118
00:07:07,123 --> 00:07:11,418
Uh, I mean he's thinking of becoming a professional hot air balloonist.

119
00:07:11,710 --> 00:07:18,008
He even wrote in an essay at school that he wanted to fly for a living.

120
00:07:18,217 --> 00:07:19,176
Didn't you?

121
00:07:19,510 --> 00:07:20,386
Umm, yeah.

122
00:07:20,803 --> 00:07:24,598
That's great. I'll teach you all you need to know.

123
00:07:24,807 --> 00:07:26,183
Thank you very much.

124
00:07:32,565 --> 00:07:34,024
I'm so hungry.

125
00:07:34,567 --> 00:07:36,861
Nobody delivers this late at night.

126
00:07:37,069 --> 00:07:39,280
I don't feel like walking to the store.

127
00:07:40,948 --> 00:07:41,740
Huh?

128
00:07:41,949 --> 00:07:42,783
What's that?

129
00:07:48,164 --> 00:07:50,499
"RAMEN"

130
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:51,792
What the heck?!

131
00:07:52,001 --> 00:07:57,798
"RAMEN CALL 030-22..."

132
00:07:58,007 --> 00:08:00,050
I think... they're selling noodles.

133
00:08:00,801 --> 00:08:01,635
No way.

134
00:08:01,886 --> 00:08:04,013
There's a phone number.

135
00:08:04,221 --> 00:08:06,056
I guess it's worth a try.

136
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:16,108
&lt;i&gt;This is Balloon Ramen.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Do you want a delivery?&lt;/i&gt;

137
00:08:16,358 --> 00:08:17,151
What?

138
00:08:17,651 --> 00:08:20,905
Uh, could we have two bowls of ramen?

139
00:08:21,113 --> 00:08:23,657
&lt;i&gt;Sure thing, two ramen.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Name and address please.&lt;/i&gt;

140
00:08:24,158 --> 00:08:27,244
I'm Yamada. Apartment 3011 of Tower A.

141
00:08:27,828 --> 00:08:30,164
&lt;i&gt;30th floor?&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Okay, thanks for your order.&lt;/i&gt;

142
00:08:30,915 --> 00:08:32,750
They took my order.

143
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,085
But how are they gonna deliver it?

144
00:08:37,671 --> 00:08:38,923
Whoa!

145
00:08:44,970 --> 00:08:46,096
It's coming closer.

146
00:08:46,305 --> 00:08:47,389
I'm scared!

147
00:08:47,932 --> 00:08:50,351
Hi there!

148
00:08:53,062 --> 00:08:54,104
You're Yamada-san?

149
00:08:54,313 --> 00:08:55,105
Y...Yes.

150
00:08:55,648 --> 00:08:57,107
The ramen's ready.

151
00:08:57,316 --> 00:08:58,734
Oh, that was fast!

152
00:08:59,401 --> 00:09:02,613
-The hot air balloon... -It's a ramen kitchen!

153
00:09:03,113 --> 00:09:03,989
Here they are.

154
00:09:04,198 --> 00:09:04,990
Okay!

155
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:06,992
Whoa!

156
00:09:07,201 --> 00:09:09,828
Thanks for waiting. That'll be 1000 yen.

157
00:09:10,037 --> 00:09:10,996
Th-thanks...

158
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:15,125
Hello, Balloon Ramen.

159
00:09:15,918 --> 00:09:17,503
Okay, thank you.

160
00:09:17,711 --> 00:09:21,048
Three bowls of ramen to Apartment 4023 of Tower B.

161
00:09:21,257 --> 00:09:24,009
Got it. It must be that apartment.

162
00:09:27,388 --> 00:09:29,848
Perfect! I'll pull us in.

163
00:09:30,891 --> 00:09:31,809
Another order!

164
00:09:32,977 --> 00:09:35,312
One extra large bowl of ramen, coming up!

165
00:09:35,521 --> 00:09:37,815
Pork ramen. That's 700 yen.

166
00:09:38,357 --> 00:09:40,818
Five miso ramen? Okay!

167
00:09:42,027 --> 00:09:44,363
Whoa, what a busy day.

168
00:09:45,531 --> 00:09:46,991
Ryo-san, there's a cop car.

169
00:09:47,616 --> 00:09:49,994
Damn it. Someone must have reported us.

170
00:09:50,202 --> 00:09:50,995
Now what?

171
00:09:51,287 --> 00:09:54,748
Execute emergency maneuvers!

172
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:57,626
That's the balloon.

173
00:09:59,128 --> 00:10:01,255
-Where'd it go? -It's too dark to see it.

174
00:10:01,755 --> 00:10:04,383
I call this "Operation Midnight Raven."

175
00:10:04,591 --> 00:10:07,511
This is why we painted the balloon black.

176
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:10,014
You've always got something up your sleeve.

177
00:10:10,389 --> 00:10:14,226
We can't get caught on day one. You'd be out of business!

178
00:10:14,810 --> 00:10:18,731
I didn't expect us to sell so much.

179
00:10:18,939 --> 00:10:24,069
If it keeps going this well, you can waive my tab as my idea fee.

180
00:10:24,278 --> 00:10:28,741
You don't miss a trick. But are cops allowed to do side work?

181
00:10:29,491 --> 00:10:33,746
A police officer has a duty to help citizens in need!

182
00:10:34,204 --> 00:10:38,751
We cannot stand by and let people go hungry at night!

183
00:10:41,086 --> 00:10:45,924
Sightings of the balloon have mainly come from around the high-rise apartments.

184
00:10:46,842 --> 00:10:49,178
It is likely to be flying again tonight.

185
00:10:49,386 --> 00:10:52,973
Redouble your patrols and do your best to find it.

186
00:10:55,684 --> 00:10:56,810
Did you hear me?

187
00:10:57,019 --> 00:11:00,230
Yes... but I don't think it'll be flying tonight.

188
00:11:00,814 --> 00:11:02,733
How do you know that?

189
00:11:02,941 --> 00:11:05,694
Because I'm the one who... Oops!

190
00:11:07,404 --> 00:11:09,740
Call it a cop's intuition.

191
00:11:10,282 --> 00:11:11,116
Hmm?

192
00:11:11,325 --> 00:11:14,244
Since you do have any cop's intuition?

193
00:11:14,453 --> 00:11:15,245
What?

194
00:11:15,621 --> 00:11:18,749
Why don't we bet on it then? 1000 yen each!

195
00:11:18,957 --> 00:11:20,250
You idiot!

196
00:11:21,377 --> 00:11:25,255
Do you think it's acceptable for upstanding police officers to gamble?

197
00:11:25,881 --> 00:11:28,133
Chief, how about this?

198
00:11:28,342 --> 00:11:32,054
If Ryo-chan manages to find the balloon,

199
00:11:32,262 --> 00:11:35,224
you let him have a day off to go to the festival.

200
00:11:35,516 --> 00:11:37,935
Hmm, that's not a bad idea.

201
00:11:38,143 --> 00:11:40,270
What do you say, Ryotsu? Any complaints?

202
00:11:40,687 --> 00:11:41,480
What?

203
00:11:41,939 --> 00:11:42,731
Hmm...?

204
00:11:44,441 --> 00:11:45,984
Okay.

205
00:11:50,739 --> 00:11:53,075
&lt;i&gt;Oh, man...&lt;/i&gt;

206
00:11:55,244 --> 00:11:59,081
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

207
00:12:01,083 --> 00:12:02,543
Good evening, sir.

208
00:12:02,876 --> 00:12:04,044
Huh?

209
00:12:04,253 --> 00:12:05,379
I'm up here!

210
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:11,009
Hey, why are you stargazing while on duty?

211
00:12:11,218 --> 00:12:12,052
I'm not.

212
00:12:13,095 --> 00:12:15,889
What then? Spying on a woman?

213
00:12:16,098 --> 00:12:18,058
Have a look for yourself.

214
00:12:18,851 --> 00:12:20,102
All right.

215
00:12:21,019 --> 00:12:23,355
What? It's just a bird.

216
00:12:23,856 --> 00:12:28,861
But how can you see it this clearly in that darkness?

217
00:12:29,319 --> 00:12:32,322
This is a starlight scope, like the US Army use.

218
00:12:32,865 --> 00:12:37,828
It will make it easy for us to find that suspicious balloon.

219
00:12:38,537 --> 00:12:40,455
This is a problem...

220
00:12:40,664 --> 00:12:43,667
Uh, I mean, this is tremendous!

221
00:12:44,042 --> 00:12:46,378
Why don't we look for the balloon together?

222
00:12:46,587 --> 00:12:48,005
We can share the credit.

223
00:12:48,213 --> 00:12:51,842
Nah, I'll let you get the glory this time.

224
00:12:53,677 --> 00:12:54,678
What?!

225
00:12:58,056 --> 00:12:59,725
Hey! What are you doing?

226
00:12:59,933 --> 00:13:01,101
Oh, hi Ryo-san!

227
00:13:01,643 --> 00:13:07,858
I thought I'd deliver you a late night snack to thank you.

228
00:13:09,484 --> 00:13:13,614
Idiot! If you people see you around here, they might get suspicious!

229
00:13:14,531 --> 00:13:16,408
Ooh, a ramen cart!

230
00:13:16,617 --> 00:13:19,786
How lucky! I was just starting to feel hungry.

231
00:13:20,537 --> 00:13:23,498
I've never eaten ramen from a food cart before.

232
00:13:23,707 --> 00:13:25,209
I'd like to try it.

233
00:13:25,959 --> 00:13:27,586
It smells so good!

234
00:13:27,794 --> 00:13:31,924
Wow, it's amazing to see inside the cart!

235
00:13:32,132 --> 00:13:33,008
What?

236
00:13:33,217 --> 00:13:36,261
Oh, this is the heir to the Nakagawa family.

237
00:13:36,470 --> 00:13:38,430
He's just working as a cop for fun.

238
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:40,933
He doesn't usually eat stuff like ramen.

239
00:13:41,350 --> 00:13:44,144
I'm not working just for fun.

240
00:13:44,311 --> 00:13:48,065
Hey, wasn't that hot air balloon also serving ramen?

241
00:13:48,273 --> 00:13:49,274
Umm...

242
00:13:51,235 --> 00:13:52,569
Your phone is ringing.

243
00:13:52,778 --> 00:13:53,820
Oh, thanks!

244
00:13:54,446 --> 00:13:56,114
Yes, hello, this is High-Fl...

245
00:13:56,365 --> 00:13:59,952
Uh, no, this is just a normal ramen cart.

246
00:14:01,286 --> 00:14:05,415
Huh? A normal ramen cart? Aren't you Balloon Ramen?

247
00:14:05,624 --> 00:14:08,043
What time are you flying by here tonight?

248
00:14:08,252 --> 00:14:11,964
Oh, sorry, we're closed today.

249
00:14:12,172 --> 00:14:15,592
Thank you. Please call again.

250
00:14:16,927 --> 00:14:19,263
Why did you say you were closed?

251
00:14:19,471 --> 00:14:24,560
Well. I was just thinking of closing early tonight.

252
00:14:25,227 --> 00:14:26,353
Right, Ryo-san?

253
00:14:26,603 --> 00:14:29,648
Don't ask me! It's none of my business.

254
00:14:29,856 --> 00:14:31,441
Oh, you're right.

255
00:14:41,410 --> 00:14:42,953
What's the password?

256
00:14:43,161 --> 00:14:44,246
"Triple somersault."

257
00:14:44,454 --> 00:14:47,666
Ah, it's you Ryo-san. I'll let you in.

258
00:14:49,710 --> 00:14:52,337
Whoa, what's all that?

259
00:14:52,546 --> 00:14:55,007
We can't rely only on ramen.

260
00:14:55,674 --> 00:14:59,136
Modern businesses need to expand in multiple directions

261
00:14:59,344 --> 00:15:01,513
to meet customers' needs.

262
00:15:01,722 --> 00:15:03,140
Oh...

263
00:15:06,852 --> 00:15:09,896
It's a flying convenience store!

264
00:15:10,105 --> 00:15:13,900
CONVENIENCE STORE AND RAMEN

265
00:15:16,903 --> 00:15:22,951
Ladies and gentlemen, Balloon Convenience Store and Ramen has arrived.

266
00:15:24,286 --> 00:15:27,080
Hello, this is Balloon Convenience Store and Ramen

267
00:15:28,081 --> 00:15:29,374
Okay, thank you.

268
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:32,294
Here you go, three bowls of pork ramen.

269
00:15:32,502 --> 00:15:34,296
Can I get a riceball as well?

270
00:15:34,504 --> 00:15:35,297
Sure!

271
00:15:35,964 --> 00:15:38,925
"Idol Hell," limited edition three-volume set.

272
00:15:39,134 --> 00:15:41,303
I've wanted this for ages!

273
00:15:41,511 --> 00:15:43,597
Do you have any cigarettes?

274
00:15:43,805 --> 00:15:44,806
Sure!

275
00:15:45,349 --> 00:15:47,434
Wow, you've got everything.

276
00:15:47,726 --> 00:15:49,311
Chocolate, please!

277
00:15:50,228 --> 00:15:52,147
Here is your tea and fried noodles.

278
00:15:52,356 --> 00:15:53,315
Thank you!

279
00:15:53,982 --> 00:15:55,692
Need some coffee?

280
00:15:56,193 --> 00:15:57,861
Shaved ice, please!

281
00:15:58,403 --> 00:16:01,698
Okay. Melon? Strawberry? Or milk?

282
00:16:02,199 --> 00:16:03,700
You saved my life!

283
00:16:03,909 --> 00:16:06,703
Oh, can I get a couple of weekly magazines too?

284
00:16:06,912 --> 00:16:07,704
Of course!

285
00:16:08,372 --> 00:16:10,207
It's non-stop!

286
00:16:10,415 --> 00:16:12,209
We're raking it in!

287
00:16:15,170 --> 00:16:16,838
-Look at that. -What?

288
00:16:17,464 --> 00:16:18,799
It's that hot air balloon.

289
00:16:19,132 --> 00:16:21,843
So it finally showed up? Let's follow it!

290
00:16:23,929 --> 00:16:27,265
This is Naoko. We've located the balloon.

291
00:16:27,808 --> 00:16:31,770
Okay. Kei-chan, prepare the starlight scope.

292
00:16:32,437 --> 00:16:33,230
Roger that.

293
00:16:35,482 --> 00:16:37,401
We're gonna be rich!

294
00:16:37,609 --> 00:16:42,364
Hello. I'm sorry, we've sold out for today.

295
00:16:42,572 --> 00:16:44,741
Thank you for calling.

296
00:16:45,826 --> 00:16:47,536
Uh-oh, it's a mini patrol car!

297
00:16:47,744 --> 00:16:48,537
What?

298
00:16:49,204 --> 00:16:52,249
Hmm! It must be Komachi and Naoko.

299
00:16:52,624 --> 00:16:57,003
Execute anti-pursuit maneuvers!

300
00:16:58,463 --> 00:16:59,506
Hey!

301
00:16:59,714 --> 00:17:01,550
They turned off the lights.

302
00:17:01,758 --> 00:17:04,928
It's okay. I can still make it out in the moonlight.

303
00:17:05,137 --> 00:17:06,138
What's that?

304
00:17:06,346 --> 00:17:08,014
It's a smoke bomb!

305
00:17:10,016 --> 00:17:14,104
How'd you like this? I call it "Operation Gone with the Mist."

306
00:17:14,312 --> 00:17:16,565
You really are cunning.

307
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:18,191
I can't see the moon.

308
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,193
Just follow the smoke!

309
00:17:20,777 --> 00:17:23,071
But I can't see the road either!

310
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,866
Damn it! Where are we driving?

311
00:17:26,074 --> 00:17:27,200
I can't see a thing!

312
00:17:30,370 --> 00:17:31,746
Stop! No!

313
00:17:32,789 --> 00:17:34,958
It's the river!

314
00:17:39,796 --> 00:17:41,089
We almost died.

315
00:17:42,841 --> 00:17:43,717
That bastard!

316
00:17:46,928 --> 00:17:48,763
It's coming this way.

317
00:17:49,681 --> 00:17:52,476
But I can't see anything.

318
00:17:52,684 --> 00:17:55,520
Why not? Isn't that a night-vision scope?

319
00:17:56,146 --> 00:17:59,191
It should have a range of several kilometers.

320
00:18:01,985 --> 00:18:04,446
Ah!! Kei-chan, look at this.

321
00:18:04,654 --> 00:18:06,490
What's wrong? Oh!

322
00:18:08,992 --> 00:18:12,662
It's been painted black. Who did this?

323
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,917
I know who does things like this.

324
00:18:19,002 --> 00:18:21,421
They aren't gonna catch us that easily!

325
00:18:22,047 --> 00:18:25,967
Thanks for helping me out even on your day off.

326
00:18:26,176 --> 00:18:28,887
We've almost made enough to pay off your debts.

327
00:18:29,763 --> 00:18:31,973
We just need one final push.

328
00:18:32,182 --> 00:18:34,768
Hello, Balloon Convenience Store and Ramen.

329
00:18:34,976 --> 00:18:36,853
&lt;i&gt;Can I order a delivery?&lt;/i&gt;

330
00:18:37,979 --> 00:18:39,105
This voice...

331
00:18:39,314 --> 00:18:40,857
&lt;i&gt;Bingo! It's Ryo-chan.&lt;/i&gt;

332
00:18:41,316 --> 00:18:46,279
Urgh, sorry we're closed for today. Night, night!

333
00:18:47,072 --> 00:18:50,158
Damn! Where did she get the phone number?

334
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:52,202
There's no doubt. It's him.

335
00:18:52,410 --> 00:18:56,790
Haven't you noticed that the balloon only appears when Ryo-chan isn't around?

336
00:18:58,250 --> 00:19:00,126
We have to stop him.

337
00:19:00,752 --> 00:19:02,879
Your colleague found out?

338
00:19:03,213 --> 00:19:07,425
Yeah, she has incredibly good intuition.

339
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:10,679
We'd better quit while we're ahead.

340
00:19:10,929 --> 00:19:13,139
Just when everything was going so well...

341
00:19:13,348 --> 00:19:17,227
Still, we should try to sell all this stuff left in the warehouse.

342
00:19:17,435 --> 00:19:21,022
Let's go out with a bang!

343
00:19:21,231 --> 00:19:24,401
You could still earn enough to open your own restaurant.

344
00:19:24,818 --> 00:19:27,279
That much? But how?

345
00:19:27,779 --> 00:19:29,781
We'll target the firework festival.

346
00:19:30,824 --> 00:19:32,409
The festival?

347
00:19:32,909 --> 00:19:34,744
Don't you have to work on that day?

348
00:19:35,787 --> 00:19:39,791
I'll make up an excuse, say someone died or something.

349
00:19:40,876 --> 00:19:43,378
I've got many elderly relatives.

350
00:19:46,214 --> 00:19:48,508
KAMEARI FIREWORK FESTIVAL

351
00:19:48,967 --> 00:19:51,011
Chief, I have something...

352
00:19:51,386 --> 00:19:54,514
I know, I know. You want the day off, right?

353
00:19:54,723 --> 00:19:56,725
Huh? Well, umm...

354
00:19:56,933 --> 00:19:58,101
I heard the report.

355
00:19:58,310 --> 00:20:03,315
It seems you've been looking for that balloon even on your days off.

356
00:20:03,565 --> 00:20:04,524
What? Uh, yeah.

357
00:20:05,025 --> 00:20:07,027
You showed passion for your work.

358
00:20:07,235 --> 00:20:10,280
I'll let you have the day off for the festival tomorrow

359
00:20:10,488 --> 00:20:11,948
Keep looking for that balloon.

360
00:20:12,157 --> 00:20:13,450
Y-yes, sir.

361
00:20:13,658 --> 00:20:15,785
What's wrong? Aren't you?

362
00:20:15,994 --> 00:20:18,079
I am! I am!

363
00:20:31,092 --> 00:20:34,429
I was looking forward to watching the fireworks.

364
00:20:34,638 --> 00:20:36,514
Why do we have to stake him out?

365
00:20:36,723 --> 00:20:39,225
Isn't it a bit strange?

366
00:20:40,018 --> 00:20:43,229
They've been standing there for ages.

367
00:20:46,942 --> 00:20:49,235
They're not moving at all?

368
00:20:49,778 --> 00:20:50,862
&lt;i&gt;It can't be!&lt;/i&gt;

369
00:20:52,989 --> 00:20:56,451
It'll take more than Reiko to stop us!

370
00:20:57,285 --> 00:21:00,121
Ryo-san, it's time for our grand finale!

371
00:21:00,330 --> 00:21:01,414
Sure is.

372
00:21:01,915 --> 00:21:05,669
Balloon Convenience Store and Ramen's closing down sale!

373
00:21:05,877 --> 00:21:09,214
We'll make it go off like fireworks!

374
00:21:09,422 --> 00:21:11,549
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen!

375
00:21:11,758 --> 00:21:15,428
Your beloved Balloon Convenience Store and Ramen has arrived!

376
00:21:16,221 --> 00:21:20,809
There's nothing quite like watching fireworks with a beer in hand.

377
00:21:21,393 --> 00:21:27,315
Enjoy your prime location with beer, snacks, and shaved ice!

378
00:21:27,983 --> 00:21:32,028
We've got everything your need for a fantastic evening!

379
00:21:32,737 --> 00:21:38,159
Let me hear you say "fireworks"!

380
00:21:42,247 --> 00:21:43,665
I'll have a beer!

381
00:21:43,873 --> 00:21:45,542
Shaved ice, please!

382
00:21:45,750 --> 00:21:47,377
Okay! Wait there!

383
00:21:50,296 --> 00:21:51,673
I knew it!

384
00:21:52,549 --> 00:21:53,633
He fooled us.

385
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:02,392
We're gonna sell out in no time!

386
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:05,395
And we'll make lots of money!

387
00:22:08,022 --> 00:22:09,232
What's wrong?

388
00:22:09,733 --> 00:22:11,735
The burners are acting up.

389
00:22:11,943 --> 00:22:13,903
It's an old balloon after all.

390
00:22:15,739 --> 00:22:18,074
Argh, it won't stop!

391
00:22:23,371 --> 00:22:25,040
Kei-chan, can you see it?

392
00:22:25,373 --> 00:22:27,125
It's just like you said.

393
00:22:31,671 --> 00:22:32,839
There's no doubt.

394
00:22:33,423 --> 00:22:35,759
So it was Ryotsu. That damn...

395
00:22:36,134 --> 00:22:37,844
idiot!

396
00:22:38,052 --> 00:22:40,597
Oh no! We're heading into the fireworks!

397
00:22:41,097 --> 00:22:43,558
Hey, what's that?

398
00:22:45,894 --> 00:22:46,895
Oh no!

399
00:22:47,604 --> 00:22:51,399
It's doing a Dutch roll due to the shockwaves.

400
00:22:51,608 --> 00:22:52,609
What a fool.

401
00:22:53,485 --> 00:22:54,402
Ryo-chan...

402
00:23:03,369 --> 00:23:05,038
Is it over?

403
00:23:05,246 --> 00:23:08,875
No, the largest two are still to come.

404
00:23:09,501 --> 00:23:10,376
There's two more?

405
00:23:11,044 --> 00:23:14,631
They're 300 meters in diameter. If we're in their path...

406
00:23:15,173 --> 00:23:16,132
What'll happen?

407
00:23:16,549 --> 00:23:18,134
They'll blow us away!

408
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,729
And that's the tragic end of a real idiot.

409
00:23:31,314 --> 00:23:32,107
Huh?

410
00:23:32,774 --> 00:23:34,067
What the heck?

411
00:23:34,275 --> 00:23:36,569
It's raining money!

412
00:23:36,778 --> 00:23:38,071
Unbelievable!

413
00:23:39,447 --> 00:23:41,533
Ryo-san... our money...

414
00:23:41,741 --> 00:23:43,618
Forget about it.

415
00:23:43,827 --> 00:23:46,454
At least we got to see the fireworks up close.

416
00:23:46,663 --> 00:23:49,415
I guess this is the price we pay for that.

417
00:23:55,255 --> 00:23:57,507
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

418
00:23:58,675 --> 00:24:01,970
ONE INCINERATED HOT AIR BALLOON

419
00:24:04,430 --> 00:24:05,557
&lt;i&gt;Yeehaw!&lt;/i&gt;

420
00:24:06,015 --> 00:24:10,562
&lt;i&gt;I've won 5.5 billion yen&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;in an overseas foreign lottery!&lt;/i&gt;

421
00:24:10,770 --> 00:24:11,855
&lt;i&gt;5.5 billion!&lt;/i&gt;

422
00:24:12,355 --> 00:24:15,525
I'll pay off my debts, buy plastic models, eat eel and steak...

423
00:24:16,067 --> 00:24:18,278
How else can I use it?

424
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:22,991
NEXT EPISODE LOTTERY GUY LUCKS OUT

425
00:24:32,917 --> 00:24:37,172
&lt;i&gt;Let's keep smiling always&lt;/i&gt;

426
00:24:37,839 --> 00:24:41,467
&lt;i&gt;Even when things go wrong&lt;/i&gt;

427
00:24:41,676 --> 00:24:45,930
&lt;i&gt;Keep a pretty smile on your face&lt;/i&gt;

428
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:51,019
&lt;i&gt;And go out as if nothing happened&lt;/i&gt;

429
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:55,023
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

430
00:24:55,231 --> 00:24:59,277
&lt;i&gt;You did nothing wrong&lt;/i&gt;

431
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,698
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

432
00:25:03,907 --> 00:25:07,410
&lt;i&gt;Just like you did before, yeah&lt;/i&gt;

433
00:25:07,911 --> 00:25:12,081
&lt;i&gt;I want you to smile always&lt;/i&gt;

434
00:25:12,624 --> 00:25:17,212
&lt;i&gt;A woman with a frown isn't pretty&lt;/i&gt;

435
00:25:17,712 --> 00:25:23,259
&lt;i&gt;So you should smile as soon as you can&lt;/i&gt;

436
00:25:24,052 --> 00:25:27,013
&lt;i&gt;It's the grown-up thing to do&lt;/i&gt;

437
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:43,863
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
